WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.790
A computer adds up a hundred
numbers before you can blink.

2
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.654
It cannot comfort a sad friend.
Fast is not the same as kind.

3
00:00:13.154 --> 00:00:17.194
Here are five sums. You and the
computer race to answer them.

4
00:00:17.414 --> 00:00:21.315
The computer finishes all five
before you have finished one.

5
00:00:21.535 --> 00:00:25.483
Every answer is right. Accurate
means right every time.

6
00:00:25.703 --> 00:00:29.371
It can sort a thousand names
before you have said one name.

7
00:00:29.591 --> 00:00:33.400
It can count every car on a
road, all day and all night.

8
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.870
A computer never gets tired
and it never gets bored.

9
00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.807
Now here are some jobs a
computer cannot do at all.

10
00:00:41.027 --> 00:00:44.556
It cannot comfort a friend who
has fallen over and is sad.

11
00:00:44.776 --> 00:00:48.074
It cannot choose a present
that Grandma will love.

12
00:00:48.294 --> 00:00:51.777
It cannot be fair when two
friends want the same toy.

13
00:00:51.997 --> 00:00:55.480
Fast is not the same as
kind. Those jobs are ours.

14
00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.045
A device is a machine
with a computer inside it.

15
00:00:59.265 --> 00:01:03.444
Two things choose a device: where
you are, and what it is for.

16
00:01:03.664 --> 00:01:06.776
A phone fits in a pocket
and works anywhere you go.

17
00:01:06.996 --> 00:01:10.804
A laptop is for lots of typing,
at a desk or on your knees.

18
00:01:11.024 --> 00:01:14.832
A desktop computer stays at
one desk with a big screen.

19
00:01:15.052 --> 00:01:17.885
A smart speaker is for
when your hands are busy.

20
00:01:18.105 --> 00:01:22.424
On the bus, the phone. Cooking
with messy hands, the speaker.

21
00:01:22.924 --> 00:01:26.314
Portable means small and light
enough to carry about with you.

22
00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:30.620
A phone is portable. A desktop
computer is not portable.

23
00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.277
A portable device goes
wherever you go, in a pocket.

24
00:01:34.497 --> 00:01:38.026
A bigger computer does more,
once you have got there.

25
00:01:38.246 --> 00:01:42.054
Which one is better? It depends
on the job you are doing.

26
00:01:42.554 --> 00:01:46.223
A robot is a machine,
programmed to move and do a job.

27
00:01:46.443 --> 00:01:50.019
In stories, robots have
feelings and find things funny.

28
00:01:50.239 --> 00:01:54.326
Fictional means made up for a
story. Those robots are fictional.

29
00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:58.493
Real robots have a program
and a job. An arm welds cars.

30
00:01:58.713 --> 00:02:02.103
A vacuum turns when it bumps.
A rover drives on Mars.

31
00:02:02.323 --> 00:02:06.271
A real robot notices the world
with sensors, not feelings.

32
00:02:06.491 --> 00:02:11.088
Real robots are more boring than
film robots, and far more useful.

33
00:02:11.588 --> 00:02:15.536
Computers are fast and accurate.
People are kind and fair.

34
00:02:15.756 --> 00:02:19.099
The place and the purpose
choose the device you use.

35
00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:23.778
Story robots feel. Real robots
have a program and a job.

36
00:02:23.998 --> 00:02:27.341
The computer wins the
sums. You win the kindness.
